From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: St0neWan9 <pawamaba@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:29:44 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: bridge: reserve the app's core keys before the page,
 as Chrome does
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Plan B138 (F5-7). PreHandleKeyboardEvent offers a fixed set of app keys
(oac_reserved_keys.h: ⌘T ⇧⌘T ⌘W ⌘D ⌘L ⌘1-9 ⌘{ ⌘} ⌥⌘↑↓ ⌃Tab ⌃⇧Tab ⌃1-9
⌥⌘←→ ⌘[ ⌘] ⌘R ⇧⌘R ⇧⌘C ⌘N ⇧⌘N ⇧⌘W ⌘, ⌘Q) to the shell before the page, so a
page's preventDefault cannot block them. A key the shell does not take goes
on to the page; other keys still reach the shell only when the page leaves
them unhandled. Nothing but ⌘Q is reserved in HTML fullscreen; held ⌘T, ⌘N,
⇧⌘N do not repeat.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
